 Range threads (plan §2 #116, #145): `range.ts` (`RangeController`) shows the review's threads as block rows inside its two read-only columns; Vue fills them through the hosts `RangeEvents.hosts` hands out, never through the editor. A thread's `ThreadPlace` has two ends: `start` (a `DiffLine`, no column) and `end` (a `ThreadLine`, whose column holds the box and the count badge). `diffOrder.ts` (pure) is GitLab's one-column order over the differences (an unchanged line once, a change's removed lines, then its added ones), built by one walk whose segments carry their difference; its `segmentAt` (a column line's unchanged stretch or its side of a difference) is the one rule for whether a line is inside a difference and for an unchanged line's partner line, and `internal/threadAnchor.ts` (`linePlace`, `anchorAt`: a column line to its place and to a `ThreadLine`) is built on it; which column and line a `ThreadLine` shows in is `ipc`'s `shownLine`; `diffOrder.ts` also gives `orderIndex`/`lineAtIndex`, `placeBetween` (the earlier of press and pointer is `start`, the later `end`, keeping its column), `shownEnd` (the pointer clamped before a collapsed run), `placeSpans` (each column's lines of a place) and `unchangedRuns` (its unchanged stretches); `threadRows.ts` (pure) groups the shown threads by the aligned place of `place.end` (a removed or added line's gap after its difference's other side, an unchanged line's after its partner; collapsed threads place no row), gives each row its `kind` (`unchanged`, `changed`, or `leftEmpty`/`rightEmpty` when the gap is on a difference's empty side) and `rowHeight` (the larger column's summed host heights); `threadField.ts` holds each column's rows and count marks from `showThreadRows` and provides one `block` widget per row (`side: 1 + k` at the end of line `place − 1`; on its empty side a row sits before line `place` with a negative side, so it joins that line's block), plus `threadAnchors` (the text bottom above and the next line's block top below each unchanged row) that `CompareFrame` merges, sorted, into its scroll anchors; `CompareFrame` measures an empty difference side from its joined block's top to its text's top, so the empty side's rows are inside the band; `threadWidget.ts` (`ThreadRowWidget`) `eq`s by row key, column and keys only, so a height change keeps its DOM; `threadHosts.ts` (`ThreadHosts`, built after the views) keeps one host per shown key for as long as the key is shown, one `ResizeObserver` on every host (disconnected hosts skipped) and on both scrollers and gutters writes the row height on both cells and calls `requestMeasure`, writes `--thread-left`/`--thread-width` on each column host (the rows are `position: sticky`), gives focus back to a field inside a host after CodeMirror re-attaches it, unless a press outside every host left that field, and reports `hovered(key | null)` from each host's `pointerenter`/`pointerleave` (the hover reaches the editor through its own hosts, never through Vue); `threadNumbers.ts` merges a `mousedown` into the number gutter (returning `true`, so `@codemirror/view` calls `preventDefault` and no text selection starts; a number starts a drag, the count badge toggles that line's threads; `pressedLine`: the empty line after a last newline and an empty column's line are no line of the file and do nothing; `lineCounts` counts by `place.end`) and draws the number plus the badge as a `lineNumberMarkers` marker; the hover icon is a `theme.css` mask from `--thread-icon`. `threadDrag.ts` (`ThreadDrag`) runs the drag with capture-phase listeners on `document` (`pointermove`, `pointerup` starts the thread through `RangeEvents.startThread`, `pointercancel` and Escape cancel, Escape taken by the drag alone), `scroll` on both scrollers and window `blur` (cancel), all removed at release, cancel and `destroy`; a pointer move or a scroll asks for one `requestAnimationFrame` (a pending one is reused, cancelled at stop), which reads the line under the last pointer position after each column's own scroll-handler measure and moves the end, and a release reads it once more; the pointer's column is the one on the pointer's side of the strip's middle, and over a thread row, a column's end or an empty column the other column's line at that height. `threadTint.ts` (`threadTint`, `showTint`, `tintOf`) is a per-column field of tinted spans (`cm-thread-tint` on lines and gutter cells; `theme.css` paints `--color-selection` mixed at 45 % with transparent, a translucent layer over the difference colours whatever the theme's alpha); the controller sets it to the union of the drag's place, every draft's and the hovered host's thread (spans joined by `foldRuns.ts` `joinSpans`, the one overlap-or-touch rule, which `columnFolds.ts` also joins its runs with), dispatching only when a column's spans differ from that column's field (`tintOf`).
 
